# sphere_arcs.cam — the waterline finish of sphere.cam re-emitted under
# `compress=arcs` (DECISIONS.md "Per-op compress: arcs-first toggle committed").
# Every constant-Z waterline ring of the hemisphere is a true circle, so each
# one collapses from a chorded G01 polyline to a single exact G03 full-circle
# block (start == end, centre I = -rho J = 0). This is the generate_passes path;
# the numbers are otherwise sphere.cam's, so the pair reads as chords-vs-arcs of
# the same surface.
#
# CONTAINED 2026-08-13 (DECISIONS.md "rim-area accounting…", slice 2):
# the stock used to stop AT this feature's base plane, so the whole
# surface stood in air and the fixture only ran because there was
# nothing to hit. The stock now stands 2mm proud of the feature's top
# (z 22) and T1 roughs the moat before the finish;
# numbers in the older comments describe the same toolpath, whose
# motion is unchanged where it touches the surface.
units mm
feed 600
plunge 200
rapid_z 25
clearance_z 40
spindle 4000

stock Box(w=100, l=80, h=47, x=0, y=0, z=22)

tool T1 Endmill(dia=12.0)
tool T9 Ballmill(dia=6.0)

feature TopDome Sphere(dia=40, x=50, y=40, z=0)

run Clear(tool=T1, profile=TopDome, stepover=8.0, stepdown=5.0, stock_to_leave=0.5)
run Copy(tool=T9, surface=TopDome, stepover=3.0, compress=arcs)
